      "spam": false,
      "value": "I could see this being highly beneficial for high density areas, and allowing people to continue using an avatar of their choice (granted it won't fix everything)\n\ngoing to the improv last night, and everyone having to chance to that robot looking thing... was highly disappointing.  I'd rather keep my individuality, than watch the show, to be honest.  \n\nI know my avatar has alot of dynamic bones, and I do have particle effects (that are activated by hand animation keys)  I do have... alot of bones, but to have an option for someone to manually turn them off, I think would be the best option.  Though I am planning on making a \"minecraft\" version of my phoenix ^-^",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
